==German==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|de|er|zählen}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ɛɐ̯ˈt͡sɛːlən/}} {{qualifier|standard; used naturally in western Germany and Switzerland}}
* {{IPA|de|/ɛɐ̯ˈt͡seːlən/}} {{qualifier|overall more common; particularly northern and eastern regions}}
* {{hyphenation|de|er|zäh|len}}
* {{audio|de|De-erzählen.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-erzählen.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|ditransitive}} to [[tell]], to [[narrate]], to [[recount]] (for example a story, to someone)
#: {{ux|de|'''Erzähl''' mir ein Märchen.|'''Tell''' me a fairytale.}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''erzählte''' mir von ihrer Kindheit.|She '''told''' me about her childhood.}}
# {{lb|de|with dative object|and|{{m|de|dass}}}} to [[tell]], to [[say]] (that something occurred)
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe dir '''erzählt''', dass meine Mutter gestorben ist.|I '''told''' you that my mother had died.}}
# {{lb|de|somewhat|informal|perhaps|_|regional}} to [[talk]] a lot; to tell nonsense; to [[gabble]]
#: {{ux|de|Wir haben den ganzen Nachmittag '''erzählt'''.|We '''talked''' the whole afternoon.}}
#: {{ux|de|Der '''erzählt''' hier wieder einen! (strong stress on “erzählen”)|This guy’s '''talking''' some [bullshit] again today!}}

